\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Transporting one Fourier mode}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{Two changes of coordinates that carry a label to the same place
differ by a change fixing the original label, as in \ref{fdip-0167}.
A field also has a value at that label. The two coordinate changes
may act differently on this value even when they give it the same
destination. Which identifications between transported values keep
track of precisely that difference?}
